  "question": {
    "text": "<p>A cylindrical adiabatic&nbsp;container of total volume&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;is divided into&nbsp;two equal parts by a conducting piston which is free to move as shown in the figure. Each part&nbsp;contains&nbsp;identical gas at pressure&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></math>.&nbsp;Initially the temperatures of the left and right parts are&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></math> and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></math> respectively. An external&nbsp;force is applied on the piston of area <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math>&nbsp;to keep the&nbsp;piston at rest. The value of external force required when thermal equilibrium is reached is</p>\r\r<p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/EM0629611.jpg\" style=\"width: 275px; height: 113px;\" /></p>\r\r<p>&nbsp;</p>\r",
    "image": null
  },
